temporarily patch record.message only if needed? Requirement \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info；同一记录随后交给完整处理器，仍须保留完整消息。\" It permits maybe setting record.message? But says same record subsequent full handler retains complete message. If mutate record.message to truncated, full handler loses. Could restore afterward, but exceptions/thread safety not ideal. Better use `copy.copy(record)` for truncation, then call super().format on copy. We can compute original message. If need truncate, create shallow copy, set copy.message and possibly copy.msg to truncated. Since `logging.Formatter.format` uses record.message. But if we copy record, exception info referencing same tuple okay. It won't mutate original message. Need set msg truncated with no args? If leave msg/args then super uses record.message already set? Actually logging.Formatter.format:\nrecord.message = record.getMessage()\nif self.usesTime(): record.asctime = ...\ns = self.formatMessage(record)\n...\nSo it computes record.message = record.getMessage() overwriting. If copy still has original msg,args, it will overwrite. Need set copy.msg = truncated_message, copy.args = () (and maybe copy.message). Then super computes truncated. But requirement can't alter shared original msg,args; copy okay. To only limit message not prefix/exception, easiest call super().format(record) first to get fully formatted `msg`, but then truncating body in formatted string requires locating record.message; multi-line and exception. Could extract message and truncate with copy before formatting. Need no duplicate getMessage? compute once.\n\nImplement:\n\ndef format(self, record):\n    message = record.getMessage()\n    max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n    if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, 'keep_full_message', None) is not True and len(message) > max_chars:\n        message = _truncate_message(message, max_chars)\n        record = copy.copy(record)\n        record.msg = message\n        record.args = ()\n        record.message = message\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    ...\nBut when not truncate and no copy, super sets record.message = original and format. That's standard behavior; okay. Yet requirement could be interpreted not modify record.msg/args; we don't. record.message is modified by standard formatter anyway. For copied record, original record.message not set in formatter path. Maybe okay. But newline alignment uses `record.message` after format; for copied record record.message is truncated. Good. For nontruncated original, as before.\n\nHowever exception handling: super().format(copy) sees copy.exc_info shared preserving. Good. Stack info shared. `keep_full_message` getattr: requirement exactly is True. `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", False) is True` works; 1 is not True (identity). Good.\n\nMarker length: \"...<omitted>...\" count 15 let's verify: ... 3 + <omitted> 9 + ... 3 = 15. Budget 32 remaining 17. ceil half = ceil(17/2)=9, tail 8 yes. Formula head=(remaining+1)//2. tail=remaining-head. truncated=message[:head]+marker+message[-tail:] if tail >0; if tail 0 message[-0:] gives whole message bug. Since min 32, remaining >=17 >0 so okay. But generic maybe safe. Validation ensures max>=32, marker 15. fine.\n\nPotential issue max_message_chars bool validation. Use isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(int) or <32.\n\nDefault handler setup: read envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS. Need import envs. This reading can raise ValueError at module import if bad env, expected. likely tests set. Repeated setup uses current cached env; creates new fmt and applies. Existing old formatter retained by references (handler formatter replaced though not \"created old formatters\" if independently created). Fine.\n\nStats: in _log_worker logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True}). Does repeated extra collision? no record new.\n\nConfig helper could be added near helpers. Requirement keep existing. Let's use `_log_max_message_chars`. Ensure int parse strict: Python int accepts whitespace and \"+32\". Fine. bool not relevant. \"空串、不能解析的字符串或小于32抛出 ValueError\". int(None) if None handled. Error text must include variable name. Descriptor wraps exception with name. But tests might call descriptor and check; wrapped includes. Could proactively include variable name in helper for clarity. If value invalid raise ValueError(f\"DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS must be an integer >= 32, got {v!r}\") then wrapper \"DEEPINFER...: DEEPINFER...\". okay. But small less than. Do that.\n\nNeed maybe int big. okay.\n\nPatch with replace_text_batch. Use expected hashes. For logger insert copy import and environment import. Apply three atomic patches? Can do each replace batch. First environ. Then logger. Then stats. Then run tests. Let's edit."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10144,"completion_tokens":2043,"total_tokens":12187,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1594},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6048},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}